+  "problem": "## Observed\n\n`badf-git` (WP-2026-0066, `DESIGNED`) proposes `wp/<CANONICAL-WORK-PACKAGE-ID>-<short-slug>` and defers branch-name enforcement \"until BADF freezes one machine WP-ID form repository-wide\" (`references/branch-pr-contract.md:36`). Measured on `main` `8673d9a` (2026-08-29), that freeze is overdue and the identity surface is split three ways:\n\n- **Machine id is already `WP-2026-NNNN` in practice** — 53/53 `work/` directories, the ledger glob (`badf_gate.py:641`), the normalizer (`WP_ID_FORMS`, `:606`), path validation (`:2441`) and id allocation (`next_wp_id`, `:2609-2614`) all assume it. But the year is a **hardcoded literal in three separate regex copies** (`badf_gate.py:605-606`, `badf_compose.py:39`, `check_pr_traceability.py:13`) plus 12 literals in the gate; nothing declares it canonical.\n- **Display label is `BADF-WP-NNNN`** — 40/40 recent squash subjects and 12/12 recent PR titles use `BADF-WP-NNNN: <outcome>`; `Work-Package:` trailers are mixed (33 `BADF-WP-`, 7 `WP-2026-`); the PR template (`.github/pull_request_template.md:16`) *asks* for the display form in the machine trailer.\n- **Branch namespace drifts** — merged PR heads: 48 `wp/`, 8 `feat/`, 2 `fix/`, 2 `chore/`, 1 `gov/` (the seven most recent are `feat/`); of the `wp/` ones, 47 carry the display id (`wp/BADF-WP-NNNN-…`) and 1 the machine id. `docs/governance/GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md:58` prescribes `wp/BADF-WP-NNNN-<slug>` — **contradicting the frozen contract's** `wp/WP-2026-NNNN-<slug>` (`branch-pr-contract.md:22,28`). The declared `research/BADF-RSR-NNNN-<slug>` namespace has never been used (0 PRs).\n- **The existing control checks the wrong things** — `check_pr_traceability.py` (BADF-MAIN-001) accepts *either* trailer form and checks neither the PR title nor the branch, so title, branch and trailer can each name a different work package and CI is green.\n\nGTGM v0.1 §6 (\"Work-Package ID … the branch's primary identity\"; \"freeze one WP-ID format before enforcing a regex\"), §8 (squash subject `BADF-WP-0061: <outcome> (#112)`), §17 **GIT-B — Identity Contract: canonical WP ID, branch/PR/commit consistency**.\n\n## Expected\n\n**Freeze one identity, three faces, one binding — and make the existing control enforce it.**\n\n1. **Canonical machine id: `WP-2026-NNNN`.** `WP-2026-` is declared a fixed **ledger namespace constant** (the ledger's genesis namespace, *not* a calendar field — no year rollover, `NNNN` continues monotonically); the literal is centralized in one place in `badf_gate.py` and imported/mirrored by `badf_compose.py` and `check_pr_traceability.py` so the three copies cannot drift. This is the id that binds: `work/<id>/`, `Work-Package:` trailer, evidence/dossier `work_package_id`, branch.\n2. **Display label: `BADF-WP-NNNN`** — permitted **only** in the PR title / squash subject (`BADF-WP-NNNN: <concise outcome>`), where `NNNN` must equal the trailer's. It is never a binding key.\n3. **Branch form: `wp/WP-2026-NNNN-<slug>`** — `<slug>` = `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*`, disposable, never an identity key; `NNNN` must equal the trailer's.\n4. **Binding: the body trailer `Work-Package: WP-2026-NNNN`** — the display form in the trailer is **refused** (it is currently accepted), with the exact canonical line printed as the fix.\n\nEnforcement lands in the **existing** control — `scripts/check_pr_traceability.py`, run by the existing CI step — per GIT-I12 (no second validator). The CI step passes the PR title and head ref as **required** arguments (`--title`, `--head-ref`; absence is a usage error, never a silent skip). Refusals are fail-closed (exit 1) and each names the exact fix.\n\n**History is not rewritten:** the ledger keeps resolving the 33 historical `Work-Package: BADF-WP-NNNN` squash commits (`ledger_landings` normalization stays); only *new PRs* must bind canonically. Doctrine is reconciled: `GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md:58` → the canonical form; the PR template → `Work-Package: WP-2026-NNNN`; `branch-pr-contract.md` states enforcement is **live from WP-2026-0070** and names this WP; the unused `research/` namespace is left declared (removing it is not this WP).\n\n**This PR is its own first subject:** branch `wp/WP-2026-0070-identity-contract`, title `BADF-WP-0070: …`, trailer `Work-Package: WP-2026-0070` — the positive control on real infrastructure.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A body with `Work-Package: WP-2026-NNNN` + `Closes #N` + sections, title `BADF-WP-NNNN: …`, head `wp/WP-2026-NNNN-<slug>` (same `NNNN`) → PASS, printing `<id> closes #N on <branch>`.\n2. Trailer in display form (`Work-Package: BADF-WP-NNNN`) → refused; the message contains the exact canonical line to paste.\n3. Title without the `BADF-WP-NNNN:` display label, or with a label whose `NNNN` ≠ trailer → refused, naming both ids.\n4. Head ref outside `wp/` (`feat/…`, `feature/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`, `gov/…`), or `wp/` with the display id, or with `NNNN` ≠ trailer, or with a non-conforming slug → refused, naming the expected form.\n5. `--title` / `--head-ref` missing → usage error (exit 2), never a pass.\n6. Each refusal branch is **load-bearing** (mutation: removing any one admits an inconsistent identity).\n7. One namespace constant: `grep -c 'WP-2026-'` across the three scripts' *regex sources* shows a single definition; the other two reference it; all three still resolve `WP-2026-0001…9999`.\n8. `ledger_landings()` on real `main` history still resolves every historical `BADF-WP-NNNN` trailer to its `WP-2026-NNNN` id (count unchanged before/after).\n9. Doc-drift guards: `GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md` names `wp/WP-2026-NNNN-<slug>` and no longer contains `wp/BADF-WP-NNNN`; the PR template's trailer line is canonical; `branch-pr-contract.md` no longer says enforcement is deferred and names WP-2026-0070.\n10. `badf-gates.yml` traceability step passes `github.event.pull_request.title` and `.head.ref`; the GIT-B PR itself passes it on the runner.\n11. No Git authority, no mutation path, no ruleset change; `badf/authority-matrix.json`, `badf/tool-registry.json`, `schemas/` unchanged; `badf-git` root stays `DESIGNED` (lockfile re-signed for the amended reference).\n12. `repo` integrity clean; G07 self-dossier bound; full `unittest discover` + composed-tree compose green in CI (stdlib only).\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_badf_traceability.py` extended; faithful-runner via the CLI)\n\n- `test_canonical_trailer_title_and_branch_pass`\n- `test_display_form_trailer_is_refused_with_canonical_fix` (inverts today's `test_legacy_wp_form_accepted`, which is retired with a comment naming this WP)\n- `test_title_without_display_label_is_refused`\n- `test_title_label_must_match_trailer_id`\n- `test_branch_outside_wp_namespace_is_refused`\n- `test_branch_with_display_id_is_refused`\n- `test_branch_id_must_match_trailer_id`\n- `test_branch_slug_must_be_lowercase_kebab`\n- `test_missing_title_or_head_ref_is_a_usage_error_not_a_pass`\n- `test_namespace_constant_is_defined_once_and_shared`\n- `test_ledger_still_resolves_historical_display_form_trailers`\n- `test_control_plane_and_template_name_the_canonical_forms`\n- `test_branch_pr_contract_declares_enforcement_live_from_this_wp`\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Renaming or rewriting any historical branch, commit subject, `work/` id or tag (GIT-I06).\n- Rebasing or force-pushing existing open branches (#122 already conforms; BARCHI-1's `WP-2026-0068` branch is notified, not touched).\n- A `scripts/badf_git.py`, a schema change to the `^WP-[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` patterns, or any GitHub ruleset/branch-name rule (platform enforcement is GIT-F).\n- Calendar-year rollover semantics — explicitly rejected in favour of a namespace constant; revisit only if a real need appears.\n- Removing the unused `research/` namespace from the control plane.\n- The read-only inspector — **GIT-C, #127**, queued behind this WP.\n\n## Risk / authority / stop conditions\n\n- Change class **C2** — a governance contract with integration implications (it changes what CI refuses for every future PR), no authority change. Independent lenses per `docs/03` (architecture, composition/integration): under a single collaborator this is the standing open condition C-1 on the G07 self-dossier — recorded, not hidden.\n- Target gate **G07**; `HUMAN_REQUIRED`.\n- Practice change for the operator's own loop: branches become `wp/WP-2026-NNNN-<slug>` and trailers `Work-Package: WP-2026-NNNN`; titles are already conformant (12/12). Every refusal prints the exact fix.\n- Stop if enforcement would require touching history, a ruleset, or any file outside: the three scripts, the workflow step, the traceability test, the PR template, `GITHUB_CONTROL_PLANE.md`, `branch-pr-contract.md`, the lockfile, and this WP's own ledger/evidence files.\n- Lean mode: **enforced** — minimality ladder stop at ⑥ (minimum change to the existing control and the existing test module; one constant, no new module).\n\n## Identity\n\n- Ledger **WP-2026-0070** · demand **BADF-DEM-0057** · this issue **GOV-0049** · phase label BADF-WP-GIT-B.\n- Branch `wp/WP-2026-0070-identity-contract` in a **linked worktree** (GIT-I04; the shared clone is used by a parallel seat).\n- Reconciles whichever work package is `LANDED_UNRECONCILED` at branch time (WP-2026-0067 now; WP-2026-0068 = BARCHI-1's `badf-solution-design` WP-SOL-A if it lands first — content-agnostic).\n- Sequence per GTGM §17: **GIT-B (this) → GIT-C (#127) → D → E → F → G → H → I → J.** The B→C inversion flagged on #127 is resolved by the operator's instruction to follow the design order.\n\nsource: GTGM v0.1 §6, §8, §17 (GIT-B) · discovered-by: BARCHI-2 assessment of badf-git on `8673d9a` · status: PROPOSED\n\n🧠 **BARCHI-2** — plan posted; engineering starts on human approval.\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
